%%report case-changed-per-month title: Cases last changed per month entity: Case chart: line x: month y: records help: Maintain a governed case record for the customer lifecycle; retain its history and verify ownership before changing business-critical values. How recently cases were touched - a falling line is a register nobody is keeping up. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', updated_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_case WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND updated_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report case-age-bands title: How recently cases were changed entity: Case chart: bar x: last_changed y: records help: Maintain a governed case record for the customer lifecycle; retain its history and verify ownership before changing business-critical values. Records by time since their last change; the oldest band is the stale tail to review or retire. sql: SELECT CASE WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '30 days' THEN 'last 30 days' WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '90 days' THEN '30 to 90 days' WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '180 days' THEN '90 to 180 days' ELSE 'older than 180 days' END AS last_changed, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_case WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY MIN(updated_at) DESC
%%report case-reported-at-per-month title: Cases by reported at entity: Case chart: line x: month y: records help: Maintain a governed case record for the customer lifecycle; retain its history and verify ownership before changing business-critical values. Cases grouped by the month of reported at, looking two years back and one ahead. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', reported_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_case WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND reported_at IS NOT NULL AND reported_at >= now() - interval '24 months' AND reported_at < now() + interval '12 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report case-resolved-at-per-month title: Cases by resolved at entity: Case chart: line x: month y: records help: Maintain a governed case record for the customer lifecycle; retain its history and verify ownership before changing business-critical values. Cases grouped by the month of resolved at, looking two years back and one ahead. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', resolved_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_case WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND resolved_at IS NOT NULL AND resolved_at >= now() - interval '24 months' AND resolved_at < now() + interval '12 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report case-completeness title: How complete cases are entity: Case chart: bar x: field y: missing help: Maintain a governed case record for the customer lifecycle; retain its history and verify ownership before changing business-critical values. For each optional field, how many cases leave it empty; the long bars are the fields nobody fills in. sql: SELECT 'contact' AS field, COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE contact_id IS NULL) AS missing FROM bus_case WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'owner', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE owner_id IS NULL) FROM bus_case WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'service queue', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE service_queue_id IS NULL) FROM bus_case WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'entitlement', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE entitlement_id IS NULL) FROM bus_case WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'resolved at', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE resolved_at IS NULL) FROM bus_case WHERE deleted_at IS NULL UNION ALL SELECT 'resolution notes', COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE resolution_notes IS NULL) FROM bus_case WHERE deleted_at IS NULL ORDER BY 2 DESC
